{"id": "L05-W1", "lane": "L05", "title": "The exchange sign: nothing forces fermions over hard-core bosons", "plain": "The axioms make each site a two-state qubit and allow one record per site. That fits fermions, and equally well \"hard-core bosons\": identical at one site, but different when two are swapped in two or three dimensions. Every route tried to force the fermion sign has failed. The one theorem that gets it assumes a fermionic (Grassmann) measure at the start.", "severity": "blocking", "status": "open", "evidence": ["docs/MINIMAL_AXIOMS_2026-06-29.md:43-83", "docs/STAGGERED_DIRAC_SUBSTEP1_STATISTICS_AGNOSTIC_NO_FORCING_NOTE_2026-05-25.md:12-18", "docs/STAGGERED_DIRAC_SUBSTEP1_STATISTICS_GL_F_CONDITIONAL_DISCRIMINATOR_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-06-10.md:6-9", "docs/SPIN_STATISTICS_FS_ADMISSION_LOCATED_EXERCISE_NOTE_2026-06-06.md:23-60", "docs/GL_F_MULTILOOP_GRADED_NET_COCYCLE_NARROW_NO_GO_NOTE_2026-06-10.md:13-25", "docs/GL_F_IDENTIFICATION_BRIDGE_DECOMPOSITION_NARROW_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-06-11.md:5-30", "docs/GL_F_RECORD_VALUE_DICTIONARY_COMMUTING_LOCK_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-01.md:4", "docs/AXIOM_FIRST_SPIN_STATISTICS_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-04-29.md:8-10", "docs/CAR_FROM_POSITIVITY_NEUTRALITY_NOTE_2026-06-02.md:32", "docs/KS_ETA_VS_JW_STRING_CAR_LOCALITY_NO_GO_NOTE_2026-06-02.md:9-10", "docs/RING_MONODROMY_DOES_NOT_FORCE_CAR_NOTE_2026-06-04.md:14", "docs/ADMISSIBILITY_RULE_THE_EXCHANGE_SIGN_IS_NOT_SUPPLIED_BY_RECORDS_BOTH_HARD_CORE_SECTORS_MEET_EVERY_AXIOM_AND_FIRST_DIFFER_IN_THE_FOURTH_MOMENT_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-24.md:30-32", ".claude/science/physics-loops/staggered-dirac-a1a2-realization-closure-20260710/NO_GO_LEDGER.md:24", "walls/L05_scratch/hardcore_vs_fermion.py", "walls/L05_scratch/flux_match.py", "walls/L05_scratch/flux_match_perN.py"], "same_as": ["L05-W2", "L05-W11", "L02-W13", "L02-W11", "L01-W9", "L03-W11", "L08-W3", "L10-W1", "L14-W13"]}
{"id": "L05-W2", "lane": "L05", "title": "Local fermions on one qubit per site: the string / extra-qubit trilemma", "plain": "With one qubit per site, a fermion hopping between neighbours in 2D or 3D needs a long chain of extra operations across the lattice (a Jordan-Wigner string). Local codes exist, but they put qubits on links, add constraints, and are not selected by the axioms. So \"fermionic\", \"local\" and \"one qubit per site\" have not been shown to hold together.", "severity": "major", "status": "open", "evidence": ["docs/LOCAL_REFERENCE_FERMION_ENCODING_OBSTRUCTIONS_AND_CONSTRUCTIVE_GRAPH_ISOMETRIES_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-14.md:6-16", "docs/LOCAL_REFERENCE_FERMION_ENCODING_OBSTRUCTIONS_AND_CONSTRUCTIVE_GRAPH_ISOMETRIES_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-14.md:519-531", "docs/LOCAL_REFERENCE_FERMION_ENCODING_OBSTRUCTIONS_AND_CONSTRUCTIVE_GRAPH_ISOMETRIES_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-14.md:625-633", "archive/notes/docs/work_history/repo/review_feedback/STATE_LOCAL_FERMIONIZATION_TOPOLOGICAL_SECTOR_TOURNAMENT_CYCLE238_NOTE_2026-07-17.md:24-56", "docs/NATIVE_EDGE_RECORD_MATTER_INSTRUMENT_AND_ENERGY_LEDGER_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-05.md:4", "docs/NATIVE_EDGE_RECORD_MATTER_INSTRUMENT_AND_ENERGY_LEDGER_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-05.md:37-41", "docs/STAGGERED_SCHEME_FORCED_BY_ONE_QUBIT_PER_SITE_LOCALITY_NARROW_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-06-06.md:36-50", "docs/KS_ETA_VS_JW_STRING_CAR_LOCALITY_NO_GO_NOTE_2026-06-02.md:29", "docs/FLAVOR_CHIRALITY_GATE_NARROWS_TO_ONE_SPIN_STATISTICS_IMPORT_2026-05-31.md:19", ".claude/science/physics-loops/free-dirac-carrier-retirement-20260717/STUCK_FANOUT.md:28-38", "docs/COMPOSITE_SITES_GIVE_THE_CARVED_MAJORANAS_AN_EXACT_CHARGE_ONE_QUBIT_PER_SITE_CANNOT_TWO_CAN_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-24.md:19-30", "walls/L05_scratch/jw_weight.py"], "same_as": ["L05-W1", "L05-W3", "L03-W11", "L06-W3", "L06-W12", "L02-W2"]}
{"id": "L05-W3", "lane": "L05", "title": "What is the fermion's local space? Mode, spin coin, or half a composite", "plain": "Different parts of the lane use the one qubit in incompatible ways: as one fermion mode (the June gate), as the two-component spin \"coin\" of a walker (September campaign, which also needs four states per site once occupation counts), or as half of a two-qubit composite (Kitaev-style networks). The axioms do not say which. The owner's \"particles are patterns of records\" reading suggests none is the fermion.", "severity": "major", "status": "possibly misframed", "evidence": ["origin/claude/toe-viability-probes-20260927:docs/TOE_VIABILITY_MAP_WHERE_THE_AXIOMS_ARE_EXPOSED_AND_THE_FASTEST_DECISIVE_TESTS_2026-09-27.md:257", "origin/claude/toe-viability-probes-20260927:docs/TOE_VIABILITY_MAP_WHERE_THE_AXIOMS_ARE_EXPOSED_AND_THE_FASTEST_DECISIVE_TESTS_2026-09-27.md:580-606", "origin/claude/toe-viability-probes-20260927:docs/TOE_VIABILITY_MAP_WHERE_THE_AXIOMS_ARE_EXPOSED_AND_THE_FASTEST_DECISIVE_TESTS_2026-09-27.md:1043-1046", "origin/claude/toe-viability-probes-20260927:docs/LATTICE_HANDEDNESS_A_FINITE_RANGE_FREE_WALKER_IS_LEFT_RIGHT_BALANCED_WHETHER_TIME_FLOWS_OR_TICKS_A_CHIRAL_FREE_TICK_NEEDS_TAILS_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-27.md:322-331", "docs/repo/DEFERRED_DECISIONS.md:121-146", "docs/STAGGERED_SCHEME_FORCED_BY_ONE_QUBIT_PER_SITE_LOCALITY_NARROW_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-06-06.md:36-50", "docs/COMPOSITE_SITES_GIVE_THE_CARVED_MAJORANAS_AN_EXACT_CHARGE_ONE_QUBIT_PER_SITE_CANNOT_TWO_CAN_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-24.md:19-30", "docs/NATIVE_EDGE_RECORD_MATTER_INSTRUMENT_AND_ENERGY_LEDGER_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-05.md:37-41", "docs/ADMISSIBILITY_RULE_ONE_RECORD_PER_SITE_IS_AN_INTERACTION_NOT_A_FREE_SEA_TWO_RECORDS_UNDER_EXCLUSION_AGAINST_FREE_ANTISYMMETRIC_AND_SYMMETRIC_PAIRS_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-22.md:29-40", "/Users/jonBridger/.claude/projects/-Users-jonBridger-Projects-Physics-baremetal-probes/memory/records-are-the-grain.md"], "same_as": ["L05-W2", "L05-W9", "L14-W4", "L03-W11", "L06-W3", "L12-W1", "L09-W1"]}
{"id": "L05-W4", "lane": "L05", "title": "Spin-1/2: how a rotation acts on the qubit is a choice, not a consequence", "plain": "The axioms give the lattice cube rotations and give each site a qubit, but do not say how a rotation acts on the qubit. Four inequivalent ways fit. Calling the qubit spin-1/2 in the physical sense (turn by 360 degrees, get a minus sign) is a further choice: a spin-blind action satisfies every constraint and gives identical numbers.", "severity": "major", "status": "priced", "evidence": ["docs/CARRIER_ATTACHMENT_CONSOLIDATES_TO_RECURRING_CHIRALITY_GATE_SHARPENING_NOTE_2026-06-06.md:11-16", "docs/CARRIER_ATTACHMENT_CONSOLIDATES_TO_RECURRING_CHIRALITY_GATE_SHARPENING_NOTE_2026-06-06.md:44-99", "docs/KOIDE_MATTER_ATTACHMENT_REDUCES_TO_KS_AUDIT_NARROW_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-06-02.md:36-40", "docs/THE_SOLDERING_MENU_FOUR_ACTIONS_OF_THE_PROPER_CUBIC_ROTATIONS_ON_QUBIT_POSSIBILITIES_AND_WHAT_EACH_LETS_FORMATION_BUILD_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-22.md:4", "docs/THE_SOLDERING_MENU_FOUR_ACTIONS_OF_THE_PROPER_CUBIC_ROTATIONS_ON_QUBIT_POSSIBILITIES_AND_WHAT_EACH_LETS_FORMATION_BUILD_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-22.md:24-40", "docs/DYNAMICS_CLAUSE_CHARGES_ARE_GAUSS_DEFECTS_NO_QUBIT_CARRIES_A_COVARIANT_CHARGE_UNDER_FULL_SOLDERING_DEFECTS_ARE_BOSONS_AND_RECORD_PHASES_ARE_PURE_GAUGE_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-24.md:4", "docs/ADMISSIBILITY_RULE_THE_EXCHANGE_SIGN_IS_NOT_SUPPLIED_BY_RECORDS_BOTH_HARD_CORE_SECTORS_MEET_EVERY_AXIOM_AND_FIRST_DIFFER_IN_THE_FOURTH_MOMENT_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-24.md:103-105", "docs/PER_SITE_SU2_SPIN_HALF_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-05-02.md:1-12", "docs/FLAVOR_SPIN_STATISTICS_FORCES_MODULO_RECONSTRUCTION_2026-05-31.md:28-29", "docs/STAGGERED_DIRAC_MINIMAL_SURFACE_KINETIC_CORNER_NONFORCING_NO_GO_NOTE_2026-07-10.md:114-116"], "same_as": ["L05-W5", "L06-W12", "L14-W7", "L04-W2", "L08-W3"]}
{"id": "L05-W5", "lane": "L05", "title": "The Dirac law itself: kinetic law, one flux bit, holonomy and time are supplied", "plain": "The axioms give no motion law. A qubit lattice can just as well move qubits by neighbour swaps, an ordinary slow non-relativistic law with one zero of the dispersion, as by the relativistic Dirac law with eight zeros. The Dirac choice is currently made by adding a class of laws, one sign bit (picked by a thermal requirement), a boundary convention and a time direction.", "severity": "blocking", "status": "priced", "evidence": ["docs/MINIMAL_AXIOMS_2026-06-29.md:114-130", "docs/MINIMAL_AXIOMS_2026-06-29.md:173-190", "docs/STAGGERED_DIRAC_MINIMAL_SURFACE_KINETIC_CORNER_NONFORCING_NO_GO_NOTE_2026-07-10.md:3-16", "docs/STAGGERED_DIRAC_MINIMAL_SURFACE_KINETIC_CORNER_NONFORCING_NO_GO_NOTE_2026-07-10.md:190-236", "docs/STAGGERED_DIRAC_REALIZATION_GATE_NOTE_2026-05-03.md:341-393", "docs/STAGGERED_DIRAC_EXERCISE_HONEST_REASSESSMENT_NOTE_2026-06-06.md:27-50", "docs/STAGGERED_DIRAC_KINETIC_CLASS_FORCING_NARROW_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-06-10.md:7-20", "docs/P_FLUX_SELECTION_VIA_FSB_K_AND_Z_CERTIFICATE_CONDITIONAL_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-06-11.md:13-45", "docs/CL3_TO_CL31_SPINOR_EXTENSION_NARROW_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-05-27.md:477-483", "docs/ANOMALY_FORCES_TIME_THEOREM.md:13-30", ".claude/science/physics-loops/staggered-dirac-a1a2-realization-closure-20260710/NO_GO_LEDGER.md:5-38"], "same_as": ["L05-W4", "L05-W6", "L05-W7", "L02-W2", "L02-W4", "L04-W6", "L04-W8", "L04-W4", "L16-W3"]}
{"id": "L05-W6", "lane": "L05", "title": "A Dirac mass: rest energy has no source in the rules", "plain": "A massless lattice walker is a supplied model. Giving it a rest energy needs an extra alternating term (a staggered mass) that nothing in the covariant rules produces. Attempts that derive one need a coupling tuned below a threshold, or a supplied time-reversal-odd term, and often give a rest energy of lattice size.", "severity": "major", "status": "open", "evidence": ["docs/ADMISSIBILITY_RULE_WHAT_CAN_GAP_THE_WALK_NO_INVARIANT_TERM_AT_ANY_REACH_CHESSBOARD_OR_AXIS_STRIPES_ON_SITES_ALTERNATING_LENGTHS_GIVE_ONE_REST_ENERGY_EXCLUSION_CAGES_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-22.md:4", "docs/ADMISSIBILITY_RULE_WHAT_CAN_GAP_THE_WALK_NO_INVARIANT_TERM_AT_ANY_REACH_CHESSBOARD_OR_AXIS_STRIPES_ON_SITES_ALTERNATING_LENGTHS_GIVE_ONE_REST_ENERGY_EXCLUSION_CAGES_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-22.md:26-36", "docs/ADMISSIBILITY_RULE_THE_AXIOMS_OWN_GENERATOR_THE_SCALAR_HOP_SPLITS_THE_EIGHT_SPECIES_INTO_FOUR_LEVELS_OF_ONE_SENSE_AND_A_STAGGERED_TERM_GIVES_THEM_MASS_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-22.md:4", "docs/ADMISSIBILITY_RULE_BOND_RATES_ALTERNATE_ON_THEIR_OWN_BELOW_A_THRESHOLD_STIFFNESS_THE_SEA_AGAINST_BLOCK_59S_BOND_LAW_GIVES_EVERY_SPECIES_ONE_REST_ENERGY_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-22.md", "docs/ADMISSIBILITY_RULE_THE_RECORD_GAS_NEVER_MAKES_THE_CHESSBOARD_A_REST_MASS_NEEDS_BINDING_GROWS_ONLY_AROUND_LOOPS_CONTENT_ORDER_GIVES_THE_WALK_NO_GAP_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-22.md", "docs/ADMISSIBILITY_RULE_THE_RECORD_GAS_DOES_MAKE_THE_CHESSBOARD_WHEN_A_RECORDED_BOND_COSTS_A_FACTOR_BELOW_NINE_OVER_62500_AND_THE_TWO_FRAMED_STATES_DIFFER_AT_EVERY_SITE_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-24.md:4-9", "docs/COMPOSITE_SITE_NETWORK_FLUX_FREE_BANDS_WITH_THE_ODD_TERM_TWO_CERTIFIED_TOUCHINGS_OF_OPPOSITE_CHARGE_BECOME_SIX_AT_KAPPA_ROOT_3_OVER_20_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-26.md:4-13", "docs/COMPOSITE_SITES_GIVE_THE_CARVED_MAJORANAS_AN_EXACT_CHARGE_ONE_QUBIT_PER_SITE_CANNOT_TWO_CAN_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-24.md:72-79", "/Users/jonBridger/.claude/projects/-Users-jonBridger-Projects-Physics-baremetal-probes/memory/fork-probe-20260922.md", "/Users/jonBridger/.claude/projects/-Users-jonBridger-Projects-Physics-baremetal-probes/memory/admissibility-induced-law-block139.md"], "same_as": ["L05-W5", "L02-W12", "L07-W11", "L14-W18", "L16-W6", "L08-W4"]}
{"id": "L05-W7", "lane": "L05", "title": "Chirality: every free local walker has a mirror twin, and a qubit has no left/right switch", "plain": "The weak force treats left- and right-handed matter differently. Every simple free lattice walker comes with a mirror twin of opposite handedness: proved for the campaign's walker (4 right + 4 left) and for any strictly local tick. A single qubit has no left/right switch either. Nothing in the framework yet makes matter chiral.", "severity": "blocking", "status": "open", "evidence": ["origin/claude/toe-viability-probes-20260927:docs/LATTICE_HANDEDNESS_A_FINITE_RANGE_FREE_WALKER_IS_LEFT_RIGHT_BALANCED_WHETHER_TIME_FLOWS_OR_TICKS_A_CHIRAL_FREE_TICK_NEEDS_TAILS_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-27.md:4", "origin/claude/toe-viability-probes-20260927:docs/LATTICE_HANDEDNESS_A_FINITE_RANGE_FREE_WALKER_IS_LEFT_RIGHT_BALANCED_WHETHER_TIME_FLOWS_OR_TICKS_A_CHIRAL_FREE_TICK_NEEDS_TAILS_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-27.md:100-160", "origin/claude/toe-viability-probes-20260927:docs/LATTICE_HANDEDNESS_A_FINITE_RANGE_FREE_WALKER_IS_LEFT_RIGHT_BALANCED_WHETHER_TIME_FLOWS_OR_TICKS_A_CHIRAL_FREE_TICK_NEEDS_TAILS_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-27.md:203-282", "origin/claude/toe-viability-probes-20260927:docs/LATTICE_HANDEDNESS_A_FINITE_RANGE_FREE_WALKER_IS_LEFT_RIGHT_BALANCED_WHETHER_TIME_FLOWS_OR_TICKS_A_CHIRAL_FREE_TICK_NEEDS_TAILS_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-27.md:299-345", "origin/claude/toe-viability-probes-20260927:docs/TOE_VIABILITY_MAP_WHERE_THE_AXIOMS_ARE_EXPOSED_AND_THE_FASTEST_DECISIVE_TESTS_2026-09-27.md:256", "origin/claude/toe-viability-probes-20260927:docs/TOE_VIABILITY_MAP_WHERE_THE_AXIOMS_ARE_EXPOSED_AND_THE_FASTEST_DECISIVE_TESTS_2026-09-27.md:647-650", "docs/NO_PER_SITE_CHIRALITY_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-05-02.md:5-13", "docs/CL3_FRAME_FREE_AMBIENT_CHIRAL_GRADING_NO_GO_NOTE_2026-06-02.md:5", "docs/CHIRAL_CONTENT_IS_THE_EPSILON_D_CHIRALITY_IMPORT_DISTINCT_FROM_ORIENTATION_NARROW_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-06-08.md:10-24", "docs/THREE_GENERATION_CHIRALITY_BOUNDARY_NOTE.md:48-76", "docs/ANOMALY_FORCES_TIME_THEOREM.md:13-30", "docs/audit/AXIOM_MINIMALITY_POLICY.md:340-350", "archive/notes/docs/DOMAIN_WALL_EDGE_CONTENT_VS_SM_CHIRAL_FERMIONS_MAP_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-07-05.md:100-190", "docs/COMPOSITE_SITE_NETWORK_FLUX_FREE_BANDS_WITH_THE_ODD_TERM_TWO_CERTIFIED_TOUCHINGS_OF_OPPOSITE_CHARGE_BECOME_SIX_AT_KAPPA_ROOT_3_OVER_20_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-26.md:4-13", "docs/COMPOSITE_SITE_NETWORK_FLUX_FREE_MIDDLE_BANDS_TOUCH_AT_TWO_EXACT_POINTS_BELOW_KAPPA_STAR_AND_SIX_ABOVE_BY_AN_INTERVAL_CERTIFICATE_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-26.md", "walls/L05_scratch/hardcore_vs_fermion.out"], "same_as": ["L05-W8", "L05-W9", "L05-W3", "L06-W15", "L04-W5", "L10-W1", "L08-W5"]}
{"id": "L05-W8", "lane": "L05", "title": "Which hand: the orientation bit is not fixed by anything", "plain": "Even if the framework produced a chiral rule, nothing says which hand nature has. The axioms name only proper rotations and are silent on reflections, so a handed law needs one extra yes/no datum. The arrow of time does not fix it. The owner has parked the question, with the standing default that neither reading is adopted.", "severity": "major", "status": "priced", "evidence": ["docs/repo/DEFERRED_DECISIONS.md:50-76", "docs/repo/DEFERRED_DECISIONS.md:121-146", "docs/FLAVOR_HANDEDNESS_IS_RK_EVEN_TIME_ARROW_INSUFFICIENT_NARROW_NO_GO_NOTE_2026-06-08.md:19-30", "docs/ADMISSIBILITY_HANDED_RULE_PSEUDOSCALAR_INVARIANT_CENSUS_AND_PARITY_ODD_RECORD_CORRELATORS_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-13.md:4", "docs/A_MIRROR_ASYMMETRIC_ADMISSIBILITY_RULE_REGISTERS_ITS_OWN_PARITY_ODD_TEXTURE_AND_NOTHING_ELSE_THE_EMERGENT_FERMIONS_MOVERS_ARE_TIME_REVERSAL_IMAGES_WITH_IDENTICAL_RECORD_LAWS_BOUNDED_NOTE_2026-09-05.md:4", "docs/A_TIME_DIRECTED_FORMATION_SWEEP_REGISTERS_THE_DIRECTION_OF_MOTION_AT_ORDER_ONE_AND_ITS_SCREW_SENSE_REGISTERS_NOTHING_THE_RECORD_SIDE_IMAGE_OF_A_CURRENT_NOT_A_CHIRALITY_BOUNDED_NOTE_2026-09-05.md:4", "docs/CHIRAL_CONTENT_IS_THE_EPSILON_D_CHIRALITY_IMPORT_DISTINCT_FROM_ORIENTATION_NARROW_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-06-08.md:10-24", "docs/REGISTRATION_REINSTATES_CHIRALITY_NO_GO_NOTE_2026-06-07.md:25-30", "docs/audit/AXIOM_MINIMALITY_POLICY.md:340-350", ".claude/science/physics-loops/chirality-correction-20260909/CORRECTION_HISTORY.md:1-8", "archive/notes/docs/RULE_ACHIRALITY_FROM_MINIMALITY_QUALIFICATION_LICENSING_LAW_ACHIRAL_STATE_FREE_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-07-04.md:1-30"], "same_as": ["L05-W7", "L08-W5", "L11-W2", "L11-W4", "L06-W15", "L10-W6"]}
{"id": "L05-W9", "lane": "L05", "title": "Doublers: eight (or sixteen) copies, protected by symmetry, with no rule to keep or remove them", "plain": "A lattice fermion of this kind comes with 8 copies in space (16 if time is also a lattice). The framework declines to remove them (it treats the lattice as physical), so they must be real particles. Nothing says which are which, what would lift them, or why the count matches nature. The walker's own symmetries keep them in exactly degenerate pairs.", "severity": "major", "status": "priced", "evidence": ["docs/THREE_GENERATION_CHIRALITY_BOUNDARY_NOTE.md:12-30", "docs/THREE_GENERATION_CHIRALITY_BOUNDARY_NOTE.md:48-76", "docs/NAIVE_LATTICE_FERMION_TWO_POWER_D_SPECIES_COUNT_NARROW_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-05-10.md:30-36", "docs/STAGGERED_DIRAC_REALIZATION_GATE_NOTE_2026-05-03.md:12-27", "docs/ADMISSIBILITY_RULE_THE_SPECIES_SYMMETRY_FORCES_ONLY_DOUBLING_EVERY_NONZERO_LEVEL_IN_A_VARYING_FIELD_IS_A_PAIR_AND_A_RATE_FIELD_KEEPS_EXACTLY_SIXTEEN_ZERO_MODES_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-24.md:4-10", "docs/EMERGENT_LORENTZ_INVARIANCE_AT_THE_DIRAC_POINT_AND_THE_TASTE_CENSUS_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-03.md:5", "docs/STAGGERED_TASTE_IS_THE_QUBIT_NO_SEPARATE_KOIDE_MULTIPLICITY_NARROW_OBSTRUCTION_NOTE_2026-06-04.md:9-16", "origin/claude/toe-viability-probes-20260927:docs/LATTICE_HANDEDNESS_A_FINITE_RANGE_FREE_WALKER_IS_LEFT_RIGHT_BALANCED_WHETHER_TIME_FLOWS_OR_TICKS_A_CHIRAL_FREE_TICK_NEEDS_TAILS_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-27.md:203-260", "origin/claude/toe-viability-probes-20260927:docs/TOE_VIABILITY_MAP_WHERE_THE_AXIOMS_ARE_EXPOSED_AND_THE_FASTEST_DECISIVE_TESTS_2026-09-27.md:738-740", "/Users/jonBridger/.claude/projects/-Users-jonBridger-Projects-Physics-baremetal-probes/memory/fork-probe-20260922.md"], "same_as": ["L05-W7", "L05-W10", "L05-W3", "L04-W8", "L12-W1", "L08-W3", "L09-W2", "L10-W8"]}
{"id": "L05-W10", "lane": "L05", "title": "Species labeling (AC_phi_lambda): which corner is which particle", "plain": "The three equal-looking corner states (the hw=1 triplet) are exchanged by a lattice rotation. Any rule built from the axioms treats them alike, so nothing names one as electron, another as muon. The labeling can only come from a convention, a rotation-breaking dynamics or measured values, and the framework has none of the last two.", "severity": "major", "status": "priced", "evidence": ["docs/STAGGERED_DIRAC_SUBSTEP4_LABELING_NO_GO_NOTE_2026-05-17.md:15-25", "docs/STAGGERED_DIRAC_SUBSTEP4_POSITIVE_RATCHET_NOTE_2026-05-10.md:1-40", "docs/STAGGERED_DIRAC_REALIZATION_GATE_NOTE_2026-05-03.md:376-380", "docs/STAGGERED_DIRAC_GATE_AC_PHI_LAMBDA_LABELING_CONVENTION_ACCEPTED_PREMISE_BRIDGE_BOUNDED_NOTE_2026-05-26.md", "docs/Z3_CHARACTER_ISOMORPHISM_WEYL_AXIS_CYCLE_ORIENTATION_OPEN_GATE_NOTE_2026-05-30.md:8-30", "docs/AC_ORBIT_OCCUPANCY_STATISTICAL_GRAIN_DERIVATION_OBLIGATION.md:8-30", "docs/audit/data/derivation_obligations.json:9-26", "docs/audit/AXIOM_MINIMALITY_POLICY.md:536-565", "docs/MINIMAL_AXIOMS_2026-06-29.md:178", ".claude/science/physics-loops/staggered-dirac-a1a2-realization-closure-20260710/NO_GO_LEDGER.md:28"], "same_as": ["L05-W9", "L08-W3", "L09-W2", "L09-W1", "L11-W6", "L09-W11"]}
{"id": "L05-W11", "lane": "L05", "title": "Relativity and positivity for the lattice fermion: the standard spin-statistics route is only partly built", "plain": "The textbook proof that spin-1/2 goes with fermion statistics needs relativity, positive energy and causality. The lattice supplies none of these exactly. The reconstruction that would produce them from the lattice has been built for the free case only, in two of three pieces, with named gaps, and depends on supporting notes that are not ratified.", "severity": "major", "status": "open", "evidence": ["docs/FREE_FIELD_OS_WIGHTMAN_RECONSTRUCTION_CONDITIONAL_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-05-30.md:346-405", "docs/FREE_SECTOR_SPIN_STATISTICS_LEVEL1_MECHANISM_AND_RECONSTRUCTION_REDUCTION_BOUNDED_NOTE_2026-05-30.md:1-40", "docs/FS_FORCED_MODULO_EMERGENT_LORENTZ_STRESS_TEST_NOTE_2026-06-06.md:1-30", "docs/FREE_SECTOR_RELATIVISTIC_QFT_SUPPORT_DIAGNOSTICS_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-06-09.md:18-35", "docs/MICROCAUSALITY_FERMIONIC_EVEN_CAR_WALK_EXPANSION_LIEB_ROBINSON_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-07-18.md:4", "docs/EMERGENT_LORENTZ_INVARIANCE_AT_THE_DIRAC_POINT_AND_THE_TASTE_CENSUS_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-09-03.md:5", "docs/FREE_STAGGERED_POLE_RESIDUE_DIRAC_CARRIER_CAR_RELABELING_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-07-17.md:1-40", ".claude/science/physics-loops/free-dirac-carrier-retirement-20260717/STUCK_FANOUT.md:40-48", "docs/SPIN_STATISTICS_FS_ADMISSION_LOCATED_EXERCISE_NOTE_2026-06-06.md:103-110", "origin/claude/toe-viability-probes-20260927:docs/TOE_VIABILITY_MAP_WHERE_THE_AXIOMS_ARE_EXPOSED_AND_THE_FASTEST_DECISIVE_TESTS_2026-09-27.md:253"], "same_as": ["L05-W1", "L05-W12", "L04-W3", "L04-W8", "L03-W10"]}
{"id": "L05-W12", "lane": "L05", "title": "Reflection positivity of the Kahler-Dirac fermion on non-uniform (curved) histories", "plain": "Fifty-three notes dated 14 August to 5 September tried to show that the staggered fermion stays a proper positive quantum theory when the lattice cells are non-uniform. Every finite test returned a table with no positive-definite pairing, and no general theorem was reached in either direction.", "severity": "minor", "status": "open", "evidence": ["docs/ADMISSIBILITY_DIRAC_KAHLER_CARRIER_REFLECTION_BLOCKER_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-08-19.md:5", "docs/ADMISSIBILITY_DIRAC_KAHLER_SECTION_FRAME_INERTIA_WALL_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-08-24.md:5-8", "docs/ADMISSIBILITY_DIRAC_KAHLER_SECTION_FRAME_INERTIA_WALL_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-08-24.md:60-100", "docs/ADMISSIBILITY_DIRAC_KAHLER_STAGGERED_HERMITIAN_PAIRING_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-08-19.md:5", "docs/ADMISSIBILITY_DIRAC_KAHLER_SITE_OS_POSITIVITY_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-08-24.md:5", "docs/ADMISSIBILITY_DIRAC_KAHLER_CLOSURE_AUDIT_TWO_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-08-21.md:1-40", "docs/ADMISSIBILITY_DIRAC_KAHLER_EMBEDDING_RESIDUES_CAMPAIGN_CLOSE_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-08-23.md:1-12", "docs/repo/DEFERRED_DECISIONS.md:176-195"], "same_as": ["L05-W11", "L14-W17", "L04-W8"]}
